  "user_request_original": "Design a chirped multilayer dielectric stack with air incidence on fused silica substrate. Stack: 10 alternating pairs of HfO2 and SiO2 (Lemarchand) (20 layers total), starting with HfO2. Layer thicknesses follow a linear chirp: each successive pair has optical thickness multiplied by a chirp factor relative to the base quarter-wave wavelength. Optimize the chirp factor and base quarter-wave wavelength to maximize average reflectance across 400-700 nm band while maximizing transmittance in 1530-1565 nm band. Layer count fixed at 20. Materials: hfo2, SiO2 (Lemarchand).",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize the thicknesses of a 20-layer HfO2/SiO2 alternating stack on fused silica to maximize average reflectance in 400-700 nm and maximize average transmittance in 1530-1565 nm under normal incidence, using coherent TMM.",
